{"title":"Mock ARML","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>Mock ARML</b> is a test written by an AoPS member, designed to mimic the format of the individual round of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=ARML\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"ARML\">ARML</a> competition. \n</p><p>Starting from 2015, trumpeter is releasing a Mock ARML every year some time from March to May of the year (some times including the full set with Team, Power, Individual, Relay, Super Relay, and Tiebreaker, other times with only Individual and Relay).\n</p>\n<ul><li>2007\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?f=348&amp;t=151670&amp;hilit=mock+arml\">Mock ARML</a></li></ul></li>\n<li>2008\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 1\">2008 Mock ARML 1</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_2\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 2\">2008 Mock ARML 2</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_3\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 3\">2008 Mock ARML 3</a></li></ul></li>\n<li>2015\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c5h1085357_2015_mock_arml\">BOGTRO's Mock ARML</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://artofproblemsolving.com/community/q1h1091511p4856454\">trumpeter's Mock ARML 2015</a></li></ul></li>\n<li>2019\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c594864h1840960_contest_over_mock_arml_a_really_mbadname_lmao\">A Really Mbadname Lmao</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c594864h1840548_contest_ended_archeon_mock_arml\">Archeon Mock ARML</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c594864h1834803_5_days_left_cmc_mock_arml_2019\">CMC Mock ARML</a></li></ul></li></ul>\n<p>The user <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/user/167643\">parmenides51</a> created organized collections of most of these mocks <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c2442143_arml_mocks\">here</a> in the AoPS community.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018100512\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.017 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 1/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6934:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018100512 and revision id 230519. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}